          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s05_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s05_c3_new_multilayer_perceptron_heads_atta",
          "text": "New multilayer-perceptron heads are attached to each patch token to predict that individual patch's rotation, capturing local detail. To prevent the network from cheating, patches are carved from a slightly larger grid and randomly cropped, so a random buffer gap sits between them and edge continuity can't give away the answer.",
          "expected_role": "result",
          "cue_keywords": [
